{
  "chapter": "reliability/failure-injection",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Every fault injection asserts the same six invariants, because 'no exception was",
    "thrown' is nearly useless when half these faults are supposed to produce a controlled",
    "failure.",
    "terminal: the run reached completed, failed, or escalated, and is not stuck.",
    "no_duplicate: every external effect happened at most once, counted rather than read",
    "back from a log.",
    "bounded: cost and turns stayed under the run's cap even on the failure path.",
    "escalated: anything unresolvable reached a human queue with the reason attached.",
    "traceable: the injected fault and the recovery are both on the trace, or a game day",
    "pages the on-call for real.",
    "contained: no authorization, tenancy, or taint boundary was crossed while degraded.",
    "answerCorrect is on every run and is never read. That is the point of the last case."
  ],
  "caps": { "costCents": 100, "turns": 20 },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "a-clean-recovery-holds-every-promise",
      "run": {
        "terminalState": "completed",
        "effects": [{ "name": "issue_credit", "count": 1 }],
        "costCents": 40,
        "turns": 9,
        "unresolved": false,
        "escalationReason": null,
        "trace": { "injectedFault": "tool_error", "recoveryRecorded": true },
        "boundaries": { "tenantPropagated": true, "taintHeld": true, "authorized": true },
        "answerCorrect": true
      },
      "result": {
        "violations": [],
        "held": ["terminal", "no_duplicate", "bounded", "escalated", "traceable", "contained"],
        "passed": true
      }
    },
